<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Myocheong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1135</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Myocheong was a Korean Buddhist monk and geomancer of the Goryeo period. He urged King Injong to move the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyongyang">Pyongyang</a>, to take the title of emperor and to defy the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a>. When his plans were rejected he led a rebellion at Pyongyang in 1135 and was killed by his own followers; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-busik">Kim Bu-sik</a> suppressed the rising in 1136.</p></div>
